; Transaction-review fixture (plan 32). Read as of TODAY = 2026-10-30, so the
; default 365-day window starts 2025-10-30 (inclusive).
;
; What is here, and which test leans on it (crates/ledgeline-core/tests/review.rs):
; - a Blue Bottle family keyed `sq blue bottle oakland` with varying store
;   numbers: three untagged unknowns in the window, one old (2024) and one
;   future-dated unknown, one ignored unknown, and categorised history
;   (coffee twice, groceries once, one reviewed) — similar + precedent;
; - a reviewed rename carrying `payee-key:` — the description suggestion;
; - a Berkeley store with no history of its own — the payee-prefix source;
; - a Netflix subscription on the Visa and a renamed `NFLX` charge — the
;   recurring source;
; - `reviewed:<date>` on an unknown (Unknowns, not Recents), `reviewed:yes`
;   with free text before it, the window boundary on both sides;
; - elided amounts on almost every transaction;
; - an include (review-2025.journal) holding in-window transactions, so a
;   batch can span two files and a read-only include can be counted.
;
; Not loaded by sample.journal's e2e: its totals must not move.

account assets:checking  ; type: C
account liabilities:visa  ; type: L
account equity:opening  ; type: E
account expenses:food:coffee  ; type: X
account expenses:food:groceries  ; type: X
account expenses:streaming  ; type: X
account expenses:unknown  ; type: X

include review-2025.journal

